WEBVTT

00:59:27.504 --> 00:59:31.607
That's really cool that you're doing that,

00:59:31.631 --> 00:59:35.111
and thank you so much
for explaining so clearly to us

00:59:35.135 --> 00:59:36.641
what the situation is.

00:59:36.665 --> 00:59:40.132
I guess I speak for
the majority of people listening

00:59:40.156 --> 00:59:44.656
to say all power to you
with pulling these threads together.

00:59:44.680 --> 00:59:46.196
Thank you, Seth.

00:59:46.220 --> 00:59:47.373
WPR: Thank you, Seth.

00:59:47.397 --> 00:59:50.026
SB: Thank you, Chris and Whitney
and the TED community

00:59:50.050 --> 00:59:52.685
for all of your support over the years.

00:59:52.709 --> 00:59:56.208
Let's continue to use
science and technology

00:59:56.232 --> 00:59:59.161
for the good of the world
to solve problems like this.

00:59:59.185 --> 01:00:00.956
CA: Brilliant, brilliant, brilliant.